From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] DIRECTOR: Preserve builtin return values for command calls

Director stores a command handler's discarded return value in `the result`.
The script-handler path already implements this, but the builtin/XObject path
only popped and warned about the value. Store non-void values consistently.

This fixes object hotspots in Star Trek: The Next Generation Interactive
Technical Manual. Its scripts receive values such as `undf,165` from the XObject
and inspect `the result` to select the close-up content.
---
 engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp
index db6ff976..8eeea178 100644
--- a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-code.cpp
@@ -1852,6 +1852,8 @@ void LC::call(const Symbol &funcSym, int nargs, bool allowRetVal) {
 			if (stackSize == stackSizeBefore + 1) {
 				if (!allowRetVal) {
 					Datum extra = g_lingo->pop();
+					if (extra.type != VOID)
+						g_lingo->_theResult = extra;
 					warning("Builtin '%s' dropping return value: %s", funcSym.name->c_str(), extra.asString(true).c_str());
 				}
 			} else if (stackSize == stackSizeBefore) {
